{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1549 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3c48f5857e8921a6a80688b3c612d6481f38235a68b3f9a27257fe3cfa455c69" :edb/db-before-t 1548 :edb/db-after-t 1549 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534861 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:13:12.304Z" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186137848 1078 #edb/ref 17592186137851 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138080 1071 "What is the value of $\\mid 4\\!\\mid \\,$?" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186138080 1071 "What is the value of $\\mid 4\\!\\mid \\,?$" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138080 1074 "The absolute value of a positive number equals the number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\mid 4\\!\\mid \\, =4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/4d/4dc8f8174b1a226b3cfeaedc9e909adce1171c9daca1833d80ca09b286115755.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186138080 1074 "The absolute value of a positive number equals the number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\mid 4\\!\\mid \\, =4\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/4d/4dc8f8174b1a226b3cfeaedc9e909adce1171c9daca1833d80ca09b286115755.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138081 1071 "Find $\\mid {-2} \\mid$." 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186138081 1071 "Find $| {-2} |.$" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138081 1074 "To find the absolute value of $-2$, we simply drop the negative sign:\n\n$$\n\\mid-2\\!\\mid=2\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/79/79429acd5f23eaca53c510a515096e419cbbf1f685868bfaa1bc8ee41498adce.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186138081 1074 "To find the absolute value of $-2,$ we simply drop the negative sign:\n\n$$\n\\mid-2\\!\\mid=2\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/79/79429acd5f23eaca53c510a515096e419cbbf1f685868bfaa1bc8ee41498adce.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138082 1071 "The point shown below represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $4$. What is the number?\n\n![](images/0e/0e8aaf68af47ecf3eadbd492af662273a68400bed20d3a5b214ec118abb6a2df.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186138082 1071 "The point shown below represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $4.$ What is the number?\n\n![](images/0e/0e8aaf68af47ecf3eadbd492af662273a68400bed20d3a5b214ec118abb6a2df.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138082 1074 "The number is *negative* because it is to the *left* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $4$, so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $4$.\n\nThe negative number at a distance of $4$ from zero is $-4$, so the number is $-4$.\n\n![](images/b0/b0d99997e27059b23342de79fc887c85b56991e1312f430f80fcf39311479ad2.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186138082 1074 "The number is *negative* because it is to the *left* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $4,$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $4.$ \n\nThe negative number at a distance of $4$ from zero is $-4,$ so the number is $-4.$\n\n![](images/b0/b0d99997e27059b23342de79fc887c85b56991e1312f430f80fcf39311479ad2.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138543 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441508 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138543 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441510 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138543 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441513 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138543 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441516 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138543 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441517 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138544 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441511 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138544 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441512 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138544 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441515 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138544 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441518 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138544 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441519 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138545 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441507 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138545 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441509 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138545 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441514 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138545 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441520 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186138603 1050 420.0 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186139150 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186139150 1071 "![](images/46/46c110dc92d254443f7046536f9384fc666d58109aada2cf78cbb1ce14c0a193.png)\n\nThe point shown above represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $5$. What is the number?" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186139150 1071 "![](images/46/46c110dc92d254443f7046536f9384fc666d58109aada2cf78cbb1ce14c0a193.png)\n\nThe point shown above represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $5.$ What is the number?" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186139150 1074 "The number is *positive* because it is to the *right* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $5,$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $5.$ \n\nThe positive number at a distance of $5$ from zero is $5$\n\n![](images/7e/7e1e41b708d66f3b3abc1e58dd49afa96d958b64d6575bcdf7f6d26168bd13ba.png)" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186139666 1064 "The **absolute value** of a number is its *distance from zero* when viewed on a number line.\n\nDistances are never negative. Therefore, the absolute value of a number is always positive or zero.\n\nLet's consider the number $-5$ and its position on a number line, shown below.\n\n![](images/30/3072e47752dc69d38f997e926092f60c24966031d0484241fa9c1133d89d1c56.png)\n\nThe **distance** between $-5$ and zero equals $5$ because $-5$ is five steps away from zero.\n\n![](images/dd/dd155b158a3457eb08a95885461d3ffbd36dd852e1b6c4e9dbda04efed749280.png)\n\nTherefore, *the absolute value of* $-5$ *equals* $5$. We write this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mid \\, {-5} \\, \\mid = 5\n$$" 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186139666 1064 "The **absolute value** of a number is its *distance from zero* when viewed on a number line. \n\nDistances are never negative. Therefore, the absolute value of a number is always positive or zero.\n\nLet's consider the number $-5$ and its position on a number line, shown below.\n\n![](images/30/3072e47752dc69d38f997e926092f60c24966031d0484241fa9c1133d89d1c56.png)\n\n \n\nThe **distance** between $-5$ and zero equals $5$ because $-5$ is five steps away from zero. \n\n![](images/dd/dd155b158a3457eb08a95885461d3ffbd36dd852e1b6c4e9dbda04efed749280.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, *the absolute value of * $-5$ *equals* $5.$ We write this as follows:\n\n$$\n| \\, {-5}  \\, |  = 5\n$$" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186139668 1064 "There is a fast way to find the absolute value of a number:\n\n- The absolute value of a positive number is equal to itself. For example,\n$\\mid 8 \\mid = 8$.\n- To find the absolute value of a negative number, we drop the negative sign. For instance,\n$\\mid {-8} \\mid = 8$." 13194139534861 17592186045417 false] [17592186139668 1064 "There is a fast way to find the absolute value of a number:\n\n- The absolute value of a positive number is equal to itself. For example, \n\n$$\n|8| = 8 .\n$$\n\n- To find the absolute value of a negative number, we drop the negative sign. For instance,\n\n$$\n| {-8} | = 8.\n$$" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186441443 1080 "-3" 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [17592186441443 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534861 17592186045417 true] [1759